	skos:note "NIST's AI system, as lmodel/nist-ai-100-1 renders it, is a machine-based system that produces outputs for given objectives, a definition NIST adapts from the OECD's, so the two are close." , "gist's System is any composite whose parts work as a whole, so it is the wider term. SPDX's AIPackage describes a system as a distributed package." ;
